id: pm-uawujr
title: Linked-test schema sandbox breaks package prepare hooks that install the PM merge driver
description: "GH-743: preserve source Git workspace identity or provide an explicit acceptance context when linked package gates invoke prepare hooks that run pm merge install."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "gh:743",linked-tests,merge-driver,packages,release-gates,sandbox
created_at: "2026-07-26T13:15:17.183Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T11:13:06.564Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T11:13:03.757Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: linked execution provides a documented safe contract for package lifecycle hooks that require source Git identity; pm merge install succeeds in the supported acceptance context without exposing the real tracker to test mutation; collision failures classify deterministically with actionable guidance; direct and linked npm pack prepare paths have parity tests; docs explain schema/tracker/auto context selection
parent: pm-u9d0
severity: high
environment: Git repositories whose package prepare hook runs pm merge install
repro_steps: Link a release gate containing npm pack --dry-run; the package prepare hook runs pm merge install while linked execution rewrites PM_PATH to an external schema sandbox.
resolution: Added protected PM_SOURCE_PM_PATH and PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT propagation while retaining isolated PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH for test mutations.
expected_result: Package integration tests can inspect or invoke the source checkout without risking writes to its real tracker.
actual_result: Child environments preserve sandbox mutation paths and expose source coordinates as fallback; explicit --pm-path/--path targets take precedence and select their owning Git repository; focused merge acceptance passes.
affected_version: 2026.7.26
component: Linked-test execution sandbox
customer_impact: Packages adopting the required field-aware merge driver cannot record their complete release gate as authoritative linked PM evidence.
